#4471 was merged on subject lines ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)):
every report whose subject sounded like a wrong date went into one ticket, "dates parse
mm/dd in eu locales". That counts the noise once, which is what the desk wanted. But the
desk's own cause logic (`src/lib/kb/causes.ts`) does not agree that it is one bug.

<Callout kind="warn">
Run the cause check over the 412 reports and they fall into <b>two</b> groups with two
different fixes. One ticket cannot track two fixes.
</Callout>

## What the cause check says

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table is built from the reports at render time, not typed here. It splits #4471 into
`parser` and `hint`, and marks `hint` as "not this ticket" — reports that were merged in on
their subject but do not share the known cause.

## The two problems

**`parser` — the shared parser reads every date month-first.** A day-first (EU) tenant's
dates come out flipped: 7 April becomes 4 July. This is the bug the desk already knows, and
it covers most of the ticket. Fix: parse each tenant's dates in that tenant's locale.
Filed as [ticket #1](https://github.com/PawPas/support-kb/issues/1); **fixed** and closed
completed (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`).

**`hint` — the `booking-v3` form hints `MM/DD/YYYY`.** Day-first users follow the hint and
type the month first; the form then stores the value the tenant's day-first way, so the date
is already wrong at entry, before the parser runs. Only `form` reports from the three
`booking-v3` tenants (alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour) land here. Fixing the parser
does **not** fix these. Fix: make the form hint match the tenant's locale.
Filed as [ticket #2](https://github.com/PawPas/support-kb/issues/2); closed **won't fix** —
the `booking-v3` form was retired, so the bad hint is gone with it.

## Resolved (desk update, 5 Oct)

The desk closed #4471 on 5 October with two outcomes, one per cause — the proof that it was
never one bug:

- `parser` → **FIXED**: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
- `hint` → **WON'T FIX**: `booking-v3` form retired.

## Why one ticket hid two bugs

The merge rule reads the **subject line**, never the body or the tenant. Two bugs produce the
same complaint — "my date is wrong" — so both flowed into #4471. Intake's `intakeTag` does not
rescue this: it guesses from the reporter's browser, and it disagrees with the real cause on
38 reports (tagged `hint` but really `parser`, and the other way round).

## Lessons

- Merge on subject to count fast, but re-check the cause before you call a ticket "known".
- A number that can be computed belongs in a component: the counts above come from
  `causes.ts`, so they cannot drift from the data.

